{%- comment -%}
  horizon-blocks Phase 12 — hz-product-recommendations host (port of stock
  Horizon v4.1.1 (68760d9) sections/product-recommendations.liquid; hz-
  filename per the host-family precedent — schema/preset names stay stock).
  Deviations:
  - The custom element is RENAMED <hz-product-recommendations> (open/close
    tags, stock :32/:187) — Dawn's assets/global.js:1177 owns the stock
    <product-recommendations> tag. The renamed element is defined by the
    adapted assets/product-recommendations.js (patched copy, its doc-header
    has the full story). Class names / ids / hydration keys keep stock
    "product-recommendations" strings — they are tag-independent.
  - Standalone-host preamble (hz-carousel/hz-product-list precedent):
    component-group.css + hz-type-variables + hz-ui-tokens.
  - Phase 13 (quick-add seam closed; round 3 = DAWN-NATIVE, Nathan ruling
    2026-07-07): quick_add SECTION setting (stock's is a THEME setting;
    hz-product-list precedent, DEFAULT FALSE = live card parity). When on,
    this host loads DAWN's quick-add assets (quick-add.css + quick-add.js +
    product-form.js — the main-collection-product-grid.liquid:13-20 grid
    pattern) and blocks/_product-card-gallery renders Dawn's per-card
    trigger + modal (snippets/hz-card-quick-add; its header carries the
    ruling). Stock's quick-add-styles / quick-add-modal-styles renders
    (:27-28) and the round-1/2 modal singleton are OUT — Horizon's
    .quick-add CSS collides with Dawn's .quick-add class, and Dawn modals
    are per-card. No mobile_quick_add setting (Dawn's trigger is always
    visible at both breakpoints). Duplicate #QuickAdd-{product.id} ids when
    a product repeats across hosts = live-equivalent (first match wins).
    The Horizon quick-add subsystem stays in-repo, unwired from M&P card
    surfaces.
  - LOCKSMITH GATE in the recommendations loop (M&P "Locksmith at call
    sites" contract; hz-product-list:107-119 pattern): the recommendations
    engine can surface preview/vip/supervip products to sessions that fail
    the lock. Gate is nil-safe for the onboarding placeholder loop (blank
    product → 'false'). With it comes the Phase-10 PREFIX-style
    <!--@list/split--> marker restructure (stock's `unless forloop.last`
    suffix marker would let a gated skip leave an empty carousel slide) and
    carousel slide_count switched from stock's recommendations.products.size
    to the POST-gate slides.size (stock overcounts gated items).
  - The appended stylesheet: the .section-resource-list grid adaptation +
    support rules copied from hz-product-list (each standalone host carries
    its own copy) + the recs-specific base.css:3795-3813 extraction with two
    documented adaptations (rgb() triplet wrap; --skeleton-opacity carried).
  - The skeleton aria-label hardcodes Horizon's English
    (accessibility.loading_product_recommendations — key absent from Dawn's
    locale files).
  - Schema/preset t: strings hardcoded to Horizon's English. Preset
    static-product-card subtree mirrors hz-product-list's Phase-11 M&P
    tuning (badges child under gallery, color_suffix + #000 title,
    title/price custom 0.75rem) so recs cards default to the live M&P look;
    preset frame values (gaps/padding/product source) stay stock.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script
  src="{{ 'product-recommendations.js' | asset_url }}"
  type="module"
  fetchpriority="low"
></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Host-owned dependencies (precedent: sections/hz-blocks-host.liquid — "future
  hosts render both"): the frozen Phase-0 engine CSS the card/text/group
  children depend on, plus the type + UI token layers. hz-product-recommendations
  is a standalone host, so it cannot rely on hz-blocks-host being on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}
